From 1f000c4de1941878e44797defe9ebbac5fae94dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garrett Brown <themagnificentmrb@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 03:49:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Fix No Disc and M3U disc changes

The disc callbacks treated "no mounted image" as an open tray, so an
empty tray could never be closed. M3U files also went through the same
read-only path as multi-disc PBP files, which blocked playlist edits.

Track the tray separately and open M3U entries as individual images.
Keep No Disc selected when entries are added or removed, check the
initial-disc path before using it, and retain the playlist title for
memory cards. Keep the CD-ROM's existing swap delay when reporting
the shell status.

Tested with the two-disc Metal Gear Solid playlist, including an empty
drive, both tray states, playlist edits and invalid initial-disc hints.
The tests also check the emulated shell status and memory-card files.
